<div class="ltx_page_main">
<div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">ring homomorphism</h1>

<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<br class="ltx_break">
<p class="ltx_p">Let <math id="p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math id="p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline"><mi>S</mi></math> be rings. A <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">ring homomorphism</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/RingHomomorphism.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/ringhomomorphism"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup></em> is a <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/function">function</a> <math id="p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:R\longrightarrow S" display="inline"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⟶</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></math> such that:</p>
<ul id="I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_itemize">•</span> 
<div id="I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p"><math id="I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b)" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math> for all <math id="I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in R" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></math></p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_itemize">•</span> 
<div id="I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p"><math id="I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a\cdot b)=f(a)\cdot f(b)" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></math> for all <math id="I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in R" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></math></p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">A <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ring isomorphism</em> is a ring homomorphism which is a <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/bijection">bijection</a>. A <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ring monomorphism</em> (respectively, <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ring epimorphism</em>) is a ring homomorphism which is an <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/injectivefunction">injection</a> (respectively, <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/surjective">surjection</a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">When working in a <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/conceptlattice">context</a> in which all rings have a <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">multiplicative identity</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/ring"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/unity"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup>, one also requires that <math id="p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1_{R})=1_{S}" display="inline"><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></math>. Ring homomorphisms which <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/satisfactionrelation">satisfy</a> this <a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/property">property</a> are called <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unital</em> ring homomorphisms.
</p>
